This repository supports the corresponding review paper on DEM depression-filling algorithms, and contains three categories of code:

1. Third‑party open-source code redistributed from original authors
We incorporate the publicly released open-source code from the following studies:
- Barnes et al. (2014) — Computers & Geosciences
- Wei et al. (2019) — Environmental Modelling & Software
- Zhou et al. (2017) — Transactions in GIS
These codes remain under their original licenses; all intellectual property belongs to the original authors. Any reuse must comply with their original license terms.

2. Independent reimplementation based on published methodology
The algorithm of Planchon & Darboux (2002) — Earth Surface Processes and Landforms
is implemented by us purely according to the published principles and descriptions.
No original source code from the authors was adopted or modified.

3. Original framework and integration code
The unified calling framework, interface wrappers, running scripts, comparison tools and auxiliary functions
are fully developed by the authors of this review paper.

